  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 219 PM EDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\n- Mostly Dry Through this Weekend\n\nHigh pressure will dominate over the next few days. A shortwave\ntrough moving through Saturday may spark off some pop-up showers\nand thunderstorms late Saturday afternoon and evening. At this\ntime it is a 20 percent chance where most if not all could remain\ndry. However with Mean MUCAPE values around 1000 J/kg and some\nmoisture present at 850 mb, do not want to rule out seeing an\nisolated thunderstorm.\n\n- Rain and Thunderstorms possible Monday Though Thursday\n\nAn upper level ridge moves in for Monday with southwest flow \ntoward the surface. These southwest winds will bring warm air \nadvection along with moisture advection. Some showers could \ndevelop earlier in the day, otherwise better chances (50 percent \nor greater) move in Monday night into Tuesday. Mean MUCAPE values \nwill be around 500 to 1000 J/kg with shear values around 35 knots \nthanks to a healthy low level jet. The timing isn't ideal for \nsevere weather, but a period to keep an eye on as we get closer. \n\nShowers could linger into Wednesday and Thursday as we remain in\nsouthwest flow until the cold front moves through and high\npressure moves in.\n\nHigh temperatures will be in the 70s with the chance for some to\nsee low 80s on Tuesday. Lows overnight are expected to be in the\n40s and 50s. Temperatures will be a little warmer in the 50s and\n60s early Tuesday morning.",
